{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-32135" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-y=-5 \\\\ 2x+3y=5\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995674/state.json" "file_sha256" "ee7d97fa0713a6e1cbcdd82a28ca32b227b8041dd7ed52a6616eced2210071e1"} {"question" "q-32135" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "This system can be written as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}].$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{1\\cdot 3-(-1)\\cdot 2}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995674/state.json" "file_sha256" "ee7d97fa0713a6e1cbcdd82a28ca32b227b8041dd7ed52a6616eced2210071e1"} {"question" "q-32135" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995674/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "810204698a78ba1cb5afaa72b36bf511cb2fa072080f2ad972c8d6a4ce865887"} {"question" "q-32135" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake