  & =\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995674/state.json" "file_sha256" "ee7d97fa0713a6e1cbcdd82a28ca32b227b8041dd7ed52a6616eced2210071e1"} {"question" "q-32136" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995674/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "810204698a78ba1cb5afaa72b36bf511cb2fa072080f2ad972c8d6a4ce865887"} {"question" "q-32136" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995674/state.json" "file_sha256" "ee7d97fa0713a6e1cbcdd82a28ca32b227b8041dd7ed52a6616eced2210071e1"} {"question" "q-32136" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x=-\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "x=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "x=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "x=\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "x=\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995674/state.json" "file_sha256" "ee7d97fa0713a6e1cbcdd82a28ca32b227b8041dd7ed52a6616eced2210071e1"} {"question" "q-32136" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x=\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995674/state.json" "file_sha256" "ee7d97fa0713a6e1cbcdd82a28ca32b227b8041dd7ed52a6616eced2210071e1"} {"question" "q-320801" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The solution to the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}5y=6 \\\\ 2x-y=-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n| $x=$ {{field-1}} |\n| --- |\n\n| |  | {{field-2}} | $-5$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $-2$ | {{field-3}} |  | |  |  |  | |  | $6$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $-7$ |  | | . |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} | $-5$ |  |  |  |\n|  | $-2$ | {{field-3}} |  |  |  |\n|  | $6$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $-7$ |  |  |  |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995674/state.json" "file_sha256" "ee7d97fa0713a6e1cbcdd82a28ca32b227b8041dd7ed52a6616eced2210071e1"} {"question" "q-320801" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "This system can be written as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}].$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{0\\cdot (-1)-2\\cdot 5}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -5 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -5 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -5 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995674/state.json" "file_sha256" "ee7d97fa0713a6e1cbcdd82a28ca32b227b8041dd7ed52a6616eced2210071e1"} {"question" "q-320801" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995674/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "810204698a78ba1cb5afaa72b36bf511cb2fa072080f2ad972c8d6a4ce865887"} {"question" "q-320801" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995674/state.json" "file_sha256" "ee7d97fa0713a6e1cbcdd82a28ca32b227b8041dd7ed52a6616eced2210071e1"} {"question" "q-320801" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{1}{10}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995674/state.json" "file_sha256" "ee7d97fa0713a6e1cbcdd82a28ca32b227b8041dd7ed52a6616eced2210071e1"} {"question" "q-320801" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995674/state.json" "file_sha256" "ee7d97fa0713a6e1cbcdd82a28ca32b227b8041dd7ed52a6616eced2210071e1"} {"question" "q-320801" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995674/state.json" "file_sha256" "ee7d97fa0713a6e1cbcdd82a28ca32b227b8041dd7ed52a6616eced2210071e1"} {"question" "q-320801" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995674/state.json" "file_sha256" "ee7d97fa0713a6e1cbcdd82a28ca32b227b8041dd7ed52a6616eced2210071e1"} {"question" "q-320801" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995674/state.json" "file_sha256" "ee7d97fa0713a6e1cbcdd82a28ca32b227b8041dd7ed52a6616eced2210071e1"} {"question" "q-102809" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}5x=1-3y \\\\ 3-4y=2x\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995674/state.json" "file_sha256" "ee7d97fa0713a6e1cbcdd82a28ca32b227b8041dd7ed52a6616eced2210071e1"} {"question" "q-102809" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}5x+3y=1 \\\\ -2x-4y=-3.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}5 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -4\\end{aligned}].$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{5\\cdot (-4)-(-2)\\cdot 3}[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{14}[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now find the solution to this system as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{14}[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995674/state.json" "file_sha256" "ee7d97fa0713a6e1cbcdd82a28ca32b227b8041dd7ed52a6616eced2210071e1"} {"question" "q-102809" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995674/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "810204698a78ba1cb5afaa72b36bf511cb2fa072080f2ad972c8d6a4ce865887"} {"question" "q-102809" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995674/state.json" "file_sha256" "ee7d97fa0713a6e1cbcdd82a28ca32b227b8041dd7ed52a6616eced2210071e1"} {"question" "q-102809" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x=-\\frac{1}{14}[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "x=-\\frac{1}{14}[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "x=-\\frac{1}{20}[\\begin{aligned}5 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "x=\\frac{1}{14}[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "x=\\frac{1}{20}[\\begin{aligned}5 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995674/state.json" "file_sha256" "ee7d97fa0713a6e1cbcdd82a28ca32b227b8041dd7ed52a6616eced2210071e1"} {"question" "q-102809" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x=-\\frac{1}{14}[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995674/state.json" "file_sha256" "ee7d97fa0713a6e1cbcdd82a28ca32b227b8041dd7ed52a6616eced2210071e1"} {"question" "q-72726" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3x-y=4 \\\\ x=-2y-1\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995674/state.json" "file_sha256" "ee7d97fa0713a6e1cbcdd82a28ca32b227b8041dd7ed52a6616eced2210071e1"} {"question" "q-72726" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3x-y=4 \\\\ x+2y=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{3\\cdot 2-(-1)\\cdot 1}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now find the solution to this system as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995674/state.json" "file_sha256" "ee7d97fa0713a6e1cbcdd82a28ca32b227b8041dd7ed52a6616eced2210071e1"} {"question" "q-