category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995674/state.json" "file_sha256" "ee7d97fa0713a6e1cbcdd82a28ca32b227b8041dd7ed52a6616eced2210071e1"} {"question" "q-320810" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995674/state.json" "file_sha256" "ee7d97fa0713a6e1cbcdd82a28ca32b227b8041dd7ed52a6616eced2210071e1"} {"question" "q-72729" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}x=-3y \\\\ 2x=3\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995674/state.json" "file_sha256" "ee7d97fa0713a6e1cbcdd82a28ca32b227b8041dd7ed52a6616eced2210071e1"} {"question" "q-72729" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}x+3y=0 \\\\ 2x=3.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}].$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{1\\cdot 0-3\\cdot 2}[\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{6}[\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now find the solution to this system as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{6}[\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995674/state.json" "file_sha256" "ee7d97fa0713a6e1cbcdd82a28ca32b227b8041dd7ed52a6616eced2210071e1"} {"question" "q-72729" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995674/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "810204698a78ba1cb5afaa72b36bf511cb2fa072080f2ad972c8d6a4ce865887"} {"question" "q-72729" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995674/state.json" "file_sha256" "ee7d97fa0713a6e1cbcdd82a28ca32b227b8041dd7ed52a6616eced2210071e1"} {"question" "q-72729" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x=-\\frac{1}{6}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "x=-\\frac{1}{6}[\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "x=-\\frac{1}{6}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "x=\\frac{1}{6}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "x=\\frac{1}{6}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995674/state.json" "file_sha256" "ee7d97fa0713a6e1cbcdd82a28ca32b227b8041dd7ed52a6616eced2210071e1"} {"question" "q-72729" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x=-\\frac{1}{6}[\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995674/state.json" "file_sha256" "ee7d97fa0713a6e1cbcdd82a28ca32b227b8041dd7ed52a6616eced2210071e1"} {"question" "e-4508" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find a solution to the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x+y=2 \\\\ 4x+3y=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995674/example-4508.json" "file_sha256" "8dbf2336da80cfbac224d2e80271fc7b3c87ddf08d14af4eef26e54b0cc12421"} {"question" "e-4508" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "This system can be written as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix $[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{aligned}]$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{3\\cdot 2-4\\cdot 1}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now find the solution to this system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the solution is $x=0$ and $y=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995674/example-4508.json" "file_sha256" "8dbf2336da80cfbac224d2e80271fc7b3c87ddf08d14af4eef26e54b0cc12421"} {"question" "e-4509" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x-3y=5 \\\\ 6y-5x=-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995674/example-4509.json" "file_sha256" "c3928bc449a629e04a71b31cd9da9f639f723ca981c395ce7ef133c12a992ec3"} {"question" "e-4509" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x-3y=5 \\\\ -5x+6y=-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $A\\mathbf{x} =\\mathbf{b}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix $[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 6\\end{aligned}]$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{6\\cdot 2-3\\cdot 5}[\\begin{aligned}6 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}6 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now find the solution to this system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}6 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-2$ and $y=-3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995674/example-4509.json" "file_sha256" "c3928bc449a629e04a71b31cd9da9f639f723ca981c395ce7ef133c12a992ec3"}] "usage" {"e-4509" [] "e-4508" []} "basis" 1062 "retractions" [[17592186091970 :question/problem "Find a solution to the system of linear equations\n\n${2x + y = 2; 4x + 3y = 6$."] [17592186091970 :question/worked-solution "This system can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix $\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA^{-1} &= \\frac{1}{3 \\cdot 2 - 4 \\cdot 1}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now find the solution to this system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx &= A^{-1}b \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the solution is $x=0$ and $y=2$."] [17592186091971 :question/problem "Solve the system of linear equations\n\n${2x - 3y = 5; 6y - 5x =-8$."] [17592186091971 :question/worked-solution "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n{2x - 3y = 5; - 5x + 6y =-8\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form\n\n$$\nA\\mathbf{x} =\\mathbf{b}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix $\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 6\\end{bmatrix}$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA^{-1} &= \\frac{1}{6 \\cdot 2 - 3 \\cdot 5}\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now find the solution to this system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx &= A^{-1}b \\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -8\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-2$ and $y=-3$."]] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
